{"question": "Can an independent Head review and then post the journal?", "raw": "{\"source_ids\": [ \"0\", \"1\", \"2\"] }", "sources": ["guide:access:2", "guide:projects:1", "guide:journal:0", "guide:access:1"], "answer": "For an unavailable action, read the reason, verify office/project selection, and ask the appropriate appointed Head or administrator to resolve access. Do not bypass restrictions from another screen.\n\nFor a planning project, the appointed Head opens Setup & activation. Review work plan, schedule and budget checks, then resolve the displayed task, office and staffing blockers before confirming activation.\n\nAuthorized Accounting users open General Journal, choose office and fiscal year, and open an entry to inspect posting metadata, memo, all accounts, debit/credit totals and record references.\n\nHead, employee and Accounting responsibilities differ. A project representative is not a permanent Head; independent review approval is not permission to settle or post journals.", "passed": false}
{"question": "Does a planning estimate approve money?", "raw": "{\"source_ids\": [ \"0\", \"1\", \"2\"] }", "sources": ["guide:publication:1", "guide:pdf:1", "guide:columns:2", "guide:publication:2"], "answer": "Drafts do not consume funds. Publishing a funded proposal reserves its approved task budgets once and creates operational allocations shown in Office Budget.\n\nReview extracted groups, task count, schedules, priorities, budget planning amounts, staffing and source totals. Source funding labels do not themselves authorize Office Budget commitments.\n\nDependencies link prerequisite work. Budget opens the task's actual funding allocation; an amount shown as from plan is planning information rather than authorized funding.\n\nDirect funding of manual/imported project tasks instead uses Set budget and Authorize work funding. In either path, check approved allocations rather than counting a planning amount as cash spent.", "passed": false}
{"question": "Does Pause stop speech synthesis?", "raw": "{\"source_ids\": [ \"0\", \"3\"] }", "sources": ["guide:voice_troubleshooting:1", "guide:live_voice:0", "guide:voice_troubleshooting:0", "guide:voice_troubleshooting:2"], "answer": "Voice needs a supported browser on localhost or HTTPS. A remote laptop sends its microphone audio through the authenticated gateway to the AI laptop, which must remain online and reachable.\n\nChoose eFlow Live at the top of Help for hands-free conversation. Speak in English and pause after the question so the turn can be transcribed, answered and read aloud.\n\nIf no words appear, check browser microphone permission, input selection and the meter. A moving meter proves capture, not successful server recognition; read speech-runtime or transcription errors.\n\nRecognition, source selection and synthesis add separate delays. Written answers may arrive before speech, and cached recordings are faster than new answers. Pausing the mic should not cancel synthesis.", "passed": true}
{"question": "How do I correct a rejected petty cash request?", "raw": "{\"source_ids\": [ \"0\", \"1\", \"3\"] }", "sources": ["guide:participation:2", "guide:participation:1", "guide:cash:1", "guide:cash:2"], "answer": "Participation approval does not automatically publish a proposal, complete tasks or authorize cash. Inspect publication and financial checks separately.\n\nWhen updates are requested, correct and save the plan, then resend required approvals. A previous approval may not cover material changes to the revised plan.\n\nThe server checks the remaining task pool and applicable office, fiscal-year, recipient and cash limits. Membership alone does not grant request, approval, release or settlement permission.\n\nA submitted request waits for its required decision and release scheduling. A request, reservation or approval message is not proof that cash was already released.", "passed": false}
